  "preference": "A",
  "rationale": "Output A is much more specific and actionable. It gives the cutoff context (2024 Shaanxi science first-tier line of 475), ranks majors by civil-service suitability, and lists Xi'an schools with estimated rank ranges and reach/match/safety tiers. It also names a clear first choice (accounting at Xi'an University of Finance and Economics, 西安财经大学) and addresses the family's finances (fees, avoiding Sino-foreign programs, financial aid). It has some likely data inaccuracies: it calls 西安文理学院, a second-tier school, a public first-tier university, and its rank ranges are estimates. Output B is generic and gives no rank matching. Several of its schools, such as 西安建筑科技大学 (Xi'an University of Architecture and Technology), 西安理工大学 (Xi'an University of Technology) and 西北政法大学 (Northwest University of Political Science and Law), may be out of reach for a rank of about 40,000. It also uses the outdated name 西安财经学院 and barely engages with the limited family budget. Overall, A is far more useful."
}
